 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Then why not try A Bite of Ottawa, it's really popular here. Then that's the one. It' well over a hundred episodes, so there's plenty to explore. It is, and it's read by the author, David Onion, who lives just outside town. He makes each episode feel like a conversation. Then try The Invention of Memory, it's just a few minutes long and very thought provoking. You've come to the right place. History can be so much more than dates and names. It's about people and how they lived.",
